# ============================================================================
# CA-TBL publication rules
# ============================================================================

# --- build artefacts, regenerable by ./ns3 build ---
/build/
/cmake-cache/

# --- oversized pre-CA-TBL sweep data ---
# Nine files at 135-136 MB each, 1.2 GB total. Above GitHub's 100 MB HARD
# rejection limit, not merely the 50 MB warning -- so this is not a preference.
# They remain on disk; nothing in the repository reads them. Git LFS is the
# mechanism if they are ever needed, but 1.2 GB exceeds the free 1 GB quota.
physics_scale_sweep_*.csv

# --- simulation output: summaries and provenance only, never traces ---
# results/ is ~13 GB, almost all trace_*.csv. Every table in the technical
# report is sourced from an arm_summary.csv (~7 rows), so shipping summaries
# plus provenance keeps every reported number reproducible at a fraction of
# the size. Traces regenerate from the seed.
/results/**
!/results/**/
!/results/**/arm_summary.csv
!/results/**/run_id.txt
!/results/**/probe_range_sweep.csv
!/results/**/*.md

# --- working directories ---
/audit/
.claude/

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Files the project's rules require to stay UNTRACKED.
#
# This list was enforced by memory until 2026-08-29, when 35466c0 tracked
# CA_TBL_HANDOFF_v4.md for the first time and aa8328b had to untrack it. A rule
# enforced by recall is not enforced. G8 in scripts/catbl_gates.sh asserts none of
# these is tracked; `git rm --cached <path>` is the remedy if one ever is.
#
# Enumerated from the project's own guardrail lists, not from recall:
#   CA_TBL_HANDOFF_v4.md   named explicitly in every guardrail block (19 documents)
#   SESSION_CHANGELOG.md   working log, never a deliverable
#
# Superseded handoffs under docs/archive/ ARE tracked and stay tracked -- the rule
# is about the LIVE working handoff, not its archived predecessors.
CA_TBL_HANDOFF_v*.md
SESSION_CHANGELOG.md
# Untracked 2026-08-29: an earlier technical report, not a deliverable. Zero ###
# section overlap with Simulation.md, cited by no deliverable, entered the index only
# as a side effect of an r80 one-liner in 35466c0. Kept on disk, annotated in its own
# header.
CA_TBL_SIMULATION_REPORT.md
# 10.7 MB and deterministic from corpus.py at seed 20260819. Its sha256 IS tracked,
# and G11 assertion 1 verifies the file against it. `git add <dir>` swept it into the
# index once; this stops that recurring.
src/catbl-propagation-study/results/corpus.json

# Demo and scratch run outputs. Holds trace_*.csv, which must never be tracked (~13 GB
# across the tree, regenerable from each directory's run_id.txt invocation).
scratchpad/
